Z||000005||terryk||04-02-2000||10:32 PM||||I just dropped the U85 radio from a Grand Am in my Fiero. Graphic equalizer. Amber back lit. I got an old radio and pulled the connector from it so the factory harness plugs in. I didn't bother with the GM adapter. <P>I had to get the antenna adapter too. Also, it needs to be spaced out 1/4" from the factory radio moutns or there is a big gap.<P>Otherwise, works fine.<P>One other point, if you have the factory sub woofer, the power antenna output from the radio wouldn't power the sub so I powered it from the switch ingition line (F-&gt;E on the factory connectors).<P>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||04-03-2000||03:57 PM||||Bam Bam,<P>Someone on here got a wire harness adapter from their local GM dealer to do just what you said. Seems like it was less than $20. Do a search for something like "CD Player"... I think there was even a part number posted.<P>David.||||reg||1
Z||000007||TheFiero64||04-03-2000||06:14 PM||||I got the harness adapter. It was 18.25 and is GM part # 16140051. It plugs right in. It also includes the antenna adapter because that connecter changed also. Good luck     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 04-03-2000).]||||reg||10
